# <type>: <short imperative description>
#
# Explain why the change is needed and any non-obvious implementation choices.
# Describe side effects or compatibility concerns.
#
# Closes #123
#
# Types:
#   feat:     New user-facing behavior, Game, or Lesson
#   fix:      Bug fix
#   docs:     Documentation only
#   test:     Add or update tests
#   refactor: Code change without a behavior change
#   style:    Formatting only
#   build:    Build system or dependency change
#   ci:       Continuous integration change
#   chore:    Other maintenance
#
# Guidelines:
#   - Use imperative mood: "add", not "added" or "adds".
#   - Keep the subject concise, lowercase, and without a trailing period.
#   - Keep each commit focused on one logical change.
#   - Add a body when the reason or impact is not obvious.
#   - Reference related issues in the footer when applicable.
